module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Extension.Cotangent.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.JacobianMinorIdeal
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Fitting.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.PolynomialCotangent

/-!
# Fitting ideals of differentials and Jacobian minors

Let `R → S` be presented by `n` generators and `m` relations `f_1, …, f_m`. The conormal
sequence `S^m → S^n → Ω_{S/R} → 0` exhibits `Ω_{S/R}` as the cokernel of the Jacobian matrix
`(∂f_j/∂x_i)`, so the `r`-th Fitting ideal of `Ω_{S/R}` is generated by the
`(n - r) × (n - r)` minors of that matrix.

For a family `f` of polynomials this ties the Fitting ideals of `Ω_{S/k}`, for
`S = k[x_1, …, x_n]/(f)`, to the Jacobian-minor ideal of Tag 0C4B of the same family read in
the power-series ring `k[[x_1, …, x_n]]`: both are the image of one ideal of minors of the
polynomial Jacobian matrix.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Curves.range_cotangentComplex_eq_span_tmul_D` — the image of the naive cotangent
  complex is spanned by the differentials of a family generating the kernel.
* `Stacks.Curves.fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_eq_minorIdeal_jacobian` — the `r`-th Fitting
  ideal of `Ω_{S/R}` is the ideal of `(n - r) × (n - r)` minors of the Jacobian matrix.
* `Stacks.Curves.jacobianMinorIdealModulo_coe_eq_map_minorIdeal` — for a polynomial family the
  Jacobian-minor ideal in a quotient of the power-series ring is the image of the polynomial
  one.
* `Stacks.Curves.jacobianMinorIdealModulo_coe_eq_map_fittingIdeal` — the Jacobian-minor ideal of
  Tag 0C4B is the image of the Fitting ideal of `Ω_{S/k}` along any ring map compatible with
  the inclusion of the polynomial ring into the power-series ring.
* `Stacks.Curves.jacobianMinorIdealModulo_coe_eq_maximalIdeal_iff` — the Jacobian condition of
  Tag 0C4C for a polynomial family, as a statement in the polynomial ring.
* `Stacks.Curves.sup_sq_eq_iff_jacobianMinorIdealModulo` — for a presentation of a `k`-algebra
  whose generators lie in a maximal ideal `p`, the Jacobian minors generate `p` modulo `p ^ 2`
  exactly when they satisfy the Jacobian condition of Tag 0C4C in the power-series model.
* `Stacks.Curves.sup_sq_eq_iff_jacobianMinorIdealModulo_of_ringEquiv` — the same when the base is
  only isomorphic to a field, the isomorphism being carried in the statement.

## Implementation notes

The cokernel description is `Algebra.Extension.exact_cotangentComplex_toKaehler` together with
`Algebra.Generators.cotangentSpaceBasis`, whose coordinates of `1 ⊗ D f_j` are the partial
derivatives `∂f_j/∂x_i`; the Fitting ideal is then computed by
`fittingIdeal_eq_minorIdeal_of_presentation`. Only the span of the image of the cotangent
complex needs proof, and it follows from the Leibniz rule because the relations die in `S`.

The polynomial presentation of the quotient is `Algebra.Presentation.naive`, whose structure map
is the quotient map, and the comparison with the power-series Jacobian is
`MvPowerSeries.pderiv_coe` together with `Stacks.Curves.minorIdeal_map_matrix`.

